1
00:00:01,292 --> 00:00:02,835
Keep yourself centered.

2
00:00:04,086 --> 00:00:05,129
Breathe.

3
00:00:06,172 --> 00:00:07,256
Very good.

4
00:00:08,758 --> 00:00:11,677
That's it. Now, just keep
your head nice and clear.

5
00:00:13,804 --> 00:00:14,847
What are you doing?

6
00:00:14,972 --> 00:00:17,934
- Jane's teaching Vega balance.
- Oh, that's useful.

7
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,019
- How long?
- Forty-three seconds.

8
00:00:20,228 --> 00:00:21,896
Don't think.

9
00:00:22,021 --> 00:00:23,064
If you have to think

10
00:00:23,189 --> 00:00:25,441
thinking about dropping
will lead to dropping.

11
00:00:25,733 --> 00:00:28,569
- What should I think about?
- Anything. S'mores.

12
00:00:28,694 --> 00:00:29,904
I love s'mores.

13
00:00:30,196 --> 00:00:33,241
Graham crackers
chocolate, marshmallows...

14
00:00:33,366 --> 00:00:35,910
- Sixty seconds.
- Toasted on a campfire.

15
00:00:36,244 --> 00:00:37,495
S'mores are better in a microwave.

16
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:40,706
It's true.

17
00:00:40,831 --> 00:00:42,166
Well, I don't even know
what to say to that.

18
00:00:42,416 --> 00:00:43,793
- Very good.
- Thank you.

19
00:00:44,293 --> 00:00:47,004
- Is Agent Teresa Lisbon here?
- Hey, I'm Lisbon.

20
00:00:47,213 --> 00:00:49,715
Julie Sandoval, US Attorney
for the Northern District.

21
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:51,008
What can I do for you?

22
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:53,928
I was upstairs getting a deposition
and I heard your name mentioned.

23
00:00:54,387 --> 00:00:57,139
- Your brother is James Lisbon?
- What about him?

24
00:00:57,431 --> 00:00:59,016
Have you spoken to him
in the last few days?

25
00:00:59,141 --> 00:01:00,893
No. What's going on?

26
00:01:01,018 --> 00:01:02,853
A warrant is being issued
for his arrest.

27
00:01:02,979 --> 00:01:04,230
I thought you'd like to know.

28
00:01:04,939 --> 00:01:05,982
What did he do?

29
00:01:06,607 --> 00:01:09,360
He's a material witness
in a federal investigation.

30
00:01:09,610 --> 00:01:12,405
A man named Nathan Barnes
was beaten to death ten days ago.

31
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:14,448
He's the son
of Judge Jacqueline Barnes.

32
00:01:14,699 --> 00:01:16,993
We think your brother may have
been in contact with the victim

33
00:01:17,118 --> 00:01:18,160
the night of the murder.

34
00:01:18,619 --> 00:01:20,746
So they were in contact.

35
00:01:21,247 --> 00:01:23,291
Arresting him
seems a little over-the-top.

36
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:26,377
- We'd prefer not to, but he fled.
- He what?

37
00:01:26,544 --> 00:01:29,130
We sent officers to your brother's house
in Oklahoma City.

38
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:30,756
He slipped out the back door.

39
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:33,718
He hasn't responded to our attempts
to communicate with him.

40
00:01:34,302 --> 00:01:37,138
- Can you reach him?
- Yeah. I think so.

41
00:01:37,513 --> 00:01:38,598
Are you not close?

42
00:01:39,890 --> 00:01:41,475
No, yeah, of cour... of course I can.

43
00:01:42,351 --> 00:01:43,603
Tell him to turn himself in.

44
00:01:44,061 --> 00:01:45,187
It'll be better that way.

45
00:01:46,105 --> 00:01:47,148
Thanks for your time.

46
00:01:51,861 --> 00:01:53,362
Yes, it's serious.

47
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:55,489
An arrest warrant is serious, Stan.

48
00:01:56,616 --> 00:01:57,867
No, it's not okay.

49
00:01:58,659 --> 00:01:59,910
What'd he say
when he called you?

50
00:02:01,579 --> 00:02:03,831
Well, if you hear from him again
tell him to call me right away.

51
00:02:05,166 --> 00:02:07,126
Stan says Jimmy called him
said he was in Chicago

52
00:02:07,251 --> 00:02:08,502
but Stan doesn't know where he is.

53
00:02:08,628 --> 00:02:09,670
Well, if he's in trouble

54
00:02:09,795 --> 00:02:11,714
he's gonna go someplace
where he feels safe.

55
00:02:12,548 --> 00:02:13,591
You know where that might be?

56
00:02:13,883 --> 00:02:15,509
My parents' old house, probably.

57
00:02:15,926 --> 00:02:16,969
Sounds right.

58
00:02:18,179 --> 00:02:19,221
Hey.

59
00:02:19,388 --> 00:02:21,223
Vega and Wylie filled me in.
Are you okay?

60
00:02:21,349 --> 00:02:22,642
Yeah. Yeah, I'm fine.

61
00:02:23,059 --> 00:02:24,101
Okay.

62
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:25,728
How many siblings do you have?

63
00:02:25,853 --> 00:02:27,271
Three brothers.
I'm the oldest.

64
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:28,773
I'm the oldest of five.

65
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:30,274
Some days, keeping them in line...

66
00:02:30,691 --> 00:02:31,817
You wanna strangle 'em.

67
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,403
All of them.
At the same time.

68
00:02:34,945 --> 00:02:35,988
I'll clear your leave.

69
00:02:36,113 --> 00:02:37,198
Take as much time
as you need.

70
00:02:37,531 --> 00:02:38,574
Are you sure?

71
00:02:38,699 --> 00:02:39,742
Go and take care
of your family.

72
00:02:43,454 --> 00:02:45,831
I have to go to Chicago
find Jimmy, bring him back here.

73
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,083
Okay.

74
00:02:50,002 --> 00:02:51,671
I should only be gone
a couple of days.

75
00:02:53,089 --> 00:02:54,799
You know, I can come with you
if you want me to.

76
00:02:54,924 --> 00:02:57,385
- That wouldn't be any fun for you.
- Fun's overrated.

77
00:02:57,718 --> 00:02:59,261
If you wanna come
you can come.

78
00:03:02,515 --> 00:03:03,557
Do you want me to?

79
00:03:06,727 --> 00:03:09,188
I would very much like it
if you came.

80
00:03:09,772 --> 00:03:11,857
All right.
Then I'm gonna come.

81
00:03:12,650 --> 00:03:13,693
We'll do it together.

82
00:03:35,045 --> 00:03:37,548
My parents bought
this house when I was three.

83
00:03:37,881 --> 00:03:39,341
I lived here
all through high school.

84
00:03:39,633 --> 00:03:41,593
I haven't been here
since my dad died.

85
00:03:49,184 --> 00:03:51,437
This has got to stir up
some feelings for you.

86
00:04:00,154 --> 00:04:02,197
Could use a lick of paint
but it's nice enough.

87
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:03,782
You don't have to be polite.

88
00:04:05,576 --> 00:04:07,494
{\an8}I never lived in a house
when I was a kid, Lisbon.

89
00:04:08,620 --> 00:04:09,788
{\an8}Little envy here.

90
00:04:12,791 --> 00:04:13,834
It's still there.

91
00:04:20,632 --> 00:04:23,343
{\an8}Stan said he was fixing the place up
so his family could move in.

92
00:04:23,469 --> 00:04:25,053
{\an8}He didn't say it was a disaster.

93
00:04:26,138 --> 00:04:27,639
{\an8}Beer and pizza...
Jimmy was here.

94
00:04:27,765 --> 00:04:29,016
{\an8}I'm gonna go call Stan.

95
00:04:29,933 --> 00:04:30,976
{\an8}Okay.

96
00:04:47,576 --> 00:04:48,786
{\an8}Hey, where's your old bedroom?

97
00:04:49,077 --> 00:04:51,163
{\an8}"It's up the stairs.
First door on your right."

98
00:05:22,653 --> 00:05:25,906
I love your, uh...
your wall graffiti there.

99
00:05:31,286 --> 00:05:32,329
Jane?

100
00:05:34,206 --> 00:05:35,541
- No.
- Jane?

101
00:05:36,250 --> 00:05:37,459
- "What's going on?"
- No.

102
00:05:41,171 --> 00:05:43,340
{\an8}- Are you okay?
- Yeah. Yeah, I'm fine.

103
00:05:43,799 --> 00:05:46,051
{\an8}- I take it that wasn't your brother.
- No.

104
00:05:50,389 --> 00:05:53,600
{\an8}Yeah. Yeah. Definitely. The drywall
will be in by the 12th.

105
00:05:53,725 --> 00:05:55,769
- Hey, Stan.
- Hey, Teresa. Come in. Come in.

106
00:05:55,936 --> 00:05:56,979
Let me finish up
with this butthole.

107
00:05:57,104 --> 00:05:58,230
I'll be right with ya.

108
00:05:58,772 --> 00:06:00,399
{\an8}- Hey.
- Hi.

109
00:06:00,524 --> 00:06:01,567
Where are your cowboy boots?

110
00:06:01,692 --> 00:06:04,611
I expected cowboy boots
on the Chicago gal living in Texas.

111
00:06:04,778 --> 00:06:06,613
Patrick, this is my sister-in-law, Karen.

112
00:06:06,738 --> 00:06:08,782
- Hi.
- Is that Joey? Hi.

113
00:06:08,907 --> 00:06:11,535
Joey's three and a half.
Him and Annie are at preschool.

114
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:12,703
This is Brian.

115
00:06:13,161 --> 00:06:14,746
And you have a newborn
as well, right?

116
00:06:14,872 --> 00:06:17,040
{\an8}Paul. He's upstairs, asleep. Thank God.

117
00:06:17,165 --> 00:06:19,167
{\an8}- So, you're Patrick.
- Yeah.

118
00:06:19,293 --> 00:06:20,669
{\an8}It's fun to meet
one of Teresa's boyfriends.

119
00:06:20,794 --> 00:06:22,337
{\an8}She ever tell you
about Woody Squire?

120
00:06:22,546 --> 00:06:25,215
{\an8}- No.
- Have you heard from our brother?

121
00:06:25,507 --> 00:06:27,217
The one who's in trouble
with the federal government?

122
00:06:27,342 --> 00:06:28,385
Do you remember him?

123
00:06:28,510 --> 00:06:30,387
Yeah, she doesn't wanna
talk about Woody Squire.

124
00:06:30,596 --> 00:06:34,182
{\an8}So, uh, Jimmy has, uh some information
about a... a murder or something?

125
00:06:34,308 --> 00:06:36,685
Yeah, a guy named Nathan Barnes.
He's the son of a judge.

126
00:06:36,977 --> 00:06:39,521
Well, Jimmy will be okay. I mean,
he's dumb but he's not stupid.

127
00:06:39,646 --> 00:06:41,148
An arrest warrant is serious, Stan.

128
00:06:42,274 --> 00:06:44,443
{\an8}Oh, damn, I thought that nap
was gonna take.

129
00:06:45,485 --> 00:06:46,862
Come on.
Let's go talk in the living room.

130
00:06:47,279 --> 00:06:49,031
So, Woody Squire...
eyeliner and a lip ring.

131
00:06:49,156 --> 00:06:51,241
He pierced himself...
got infected right before prom.

132
00:06:51,366 --> 00:06:52,409
Swole up like a tennis ball.

133
00:06:52,868 --> 00:06:54,536
{\an8}- Ask her.
- Hilarious, Stan.

134
00:06:56,038 --> 00:06:58,916
{\an8}Uh, Jimmy called three days ago.

135
00:06:59,374 --> 00:07:02,169
{\an8}He said that I might hear from
some people that he was in town

136
00:07:02,294 --> 00:07:04,755
{\an8}but if anyone asked, I should
say I don't know where he is.

137
00:07:04,963 --> 00:07:06,548
And you didn't think
that was suspicious?

138
00:07:08,050 --> 00:07:10,802
I figured whatever Jimmy
got into, he could handle it.

139
00:07:11,553 --> 00:07:12,846
Not all of us are cops, T.

140
00:07:13,388 --> 00:07:14,473
And was anybody with him?

141
00:07:14,723 --> 00:07:16,433
We went to Mom and Dad's house
to look for him

142
00:07:16,558 --> 00:07:17,768
and somebody jumped Jane.

143
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:20,312
{\an8}- Holy crap. You okay?
- Oh, yeah.

144
00:07:20,437 --> 00:07:21,939
{\an8}Right as rain. Thanks.

145
00:07:22,356 --> 00:07:24,983
Wait, so this... this person
was, like, in the house.

146
00:07:25,192 --> 00:07:26,485
You have any idea who it was?

147
00:07:27,986 --> 00:07:29,446
No. I... I mean...

148
00:07:30,781 --> 00:07:32,491
It must've been
somebody looking for Jimmy.

149
00:07:33,283 --> 00:07:34,743
Uh, you know
he's playing cards again?

150
00:07:34,910 --> 00:07:36,954
Great. Great.
So you think it's a poker thing?

151
00:07:37,621 --> 00:07:39,581
Somebody's after Jimmy
to collect a gambling debt?

152
00:07:40,415 --> 00:07:41,667
Definite possibility.

153
00:07:42,626 --> 00:07:44,169
So, how's, uh...
how's business, Stan?

154
00:07:44,294 --> 00:07:45,629
You're a... you're a contractor?

155
00:07:45,837 --> 00:07:47,965
Yeah. Well, home-remodeling contractor.

156
00:07:48,090 --> 00:07:50,717
- You know, kitchens, bathrooms.
- Nice. How's that going for you?

157
00:07:51,343 --> 00:07:54,262
Things have been great.
Yeah, money's awesome.

158
00:07:54,471 --> 00:07:55,514
Yeah.

159
00:07:55,639 --> 00:07:57,599
I guess that explains why you haven't been
out to your parents' place.

160
00:07:58,141 --> 00:07:59,184
That's a nice, little place.

161
00:07:59,559 --> 00:08:00,936
Needs a little TLC, though.

162
00:08:01,728 --> 00:08:02,896
Yeah, I've been swamped.

163
00:08:03,063 --> 00:08:05,899
- Can we get back to Jimmy?
- Oh, absolutely, boss.

164
00:08:07,234 --> 00:08:08,485
Uh, so what can I do?

165
00:08:08,652 --> 00:08:10,487
Call his friends. See if any
of them have heard from him.

166
00:08:10,612 --> 00:08:12,155
We're gonna check out the bars
in Bridgeport.

167
00:08:12,447 --> 00:08:13,490
Sure.

168
00:08:13,949 --> 00:08:16,410
Oh, I forgot. Uh, baby's
christening's on Saturday.

169
00:08:16,952 --> 00:08:18,453
- Any chance you can make it?
- I'll try.

170
00:08:19,454 --> 00:08:20,956
- Got it.
- What?

171
00:08:21,498 --> 00:08:23,792
T, we all know with you
"I'll try," means, "I won't".

172
00:08:24,167 --> 00:08:26,128
Look, I'd like to come.
It's just I got a job.

173
00:08:26,294 --> 00:08:27,379
I got a job, too.

174
00:08:27,921 --> 00:08:29,756
You're not the only busy person
on the planet.

175
00:08:33,427 --> 00:08:34,469
It's fine. Hey...

176
00:08:35,721 --> 00:08:36,763
Let me know if you can make it
all right?

177
00:08:36,888 --> 00:08:37,931
I will. Yeah.

178
00:08:38,056 --> 00:08:39,558
- Patrick, nice meeting you.
- You, too.

179
00:08:39,725 --> 00:08:40,767
All right.

180
00:08:43,628 --> 00:08:45,755
I'm sorry.
My family is messy.

181
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:46,923
Oh, no need.

182
00:08:47,048 --> 00:08:49,092
- Messy people are good people.
- I'm not messy.

183
00:08:49,801 --> 00:08:51,219
You're messy on the inside.

184
00:08:53,096 --> 00:08:54,139
Wylie, what's up?

185
00:08:54,264 --> 00:08:56,182
Hey, I talked to a friend
of mine in the Dallas office

186
00:08:56,307 --> 00:08:57,851
got some info
on the Nathan Barnes murder.

187
00:08:57,976 --> 00:08:59,018
What'd you find out?

188
00:08:59,352 --> 00:09:01,020
They found his body in an alley

189
00:09:01,187 --> 00:09:03,648
behind the Wrightwood Hotel
in Dallas ten days ago.

190
00:09:03,773 --> 00:09:05,108
He'd been beaten to death.

191
00:09:05,275 --> 00:09:07,235
The ME found bruising
and cracked ribs

192
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:08,486
in addition to a busted skull.

193
00:09:08,778 --> 00:09:10,613
That doesn't sound like
a robbery gone wrong.

194
00:09:10,822 --> 00:09:13,074
"Well, he did a lot of pro-bono
work for battered women."

195
00:09:13,283 --> 00:09:16,161
Dallas cops think it was probably
an angry boyfriend or husband.

196
00:09:16,327 --> 00:09:17,829
Well, why do they want
to talk to Jimmy about it?

197
00:09:17,996 --> 00:09:20,748
Well, apparently, they found his
business card in Barnes' pocket.

198
00:09:20,999 --> 00:09:22,750
That's weird.
All right, thanks.

199
00:09:22,876 --> 00:09:23,918
Ah ah, don't hang up.

200
00:09:24,711 --> 00:09:25,753
Thank you.

201
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:27,922
Wylie, it's Jane.

202
00:09:28,548 --> 00:09:31,676
Yeah, I got in a little tussle with someone
when we first got here.

203
00:09:31,801 --> 00:09:33,720
"Could you run a description
see what comes up?"

204
00:09:34,179 --> 00:09:35,555
Yeah, sure.
Uh, hit me.

205
00:09:36,014 --> 00:09:40,643
Male, Caucasian, hazel eyes,
brown hair, mustache, beard

206
00:09:40,768 --> 00:09:46,191
"about 25 or 26 years old
6'4", 210 pounds"

207
00:09:46,566 --> 00:09:49,652
an inch-long scar running
vertically under the left eye

208
00:09:50,069 --> 00:09:53,156
and a tattoo of a spider
on the inner-right wrist.

209
00:09:53,406 --> 00:09:55,700
That is pretty detailed.
Anything else?

210
00:09:55,992 --> 00:09:58,786
Yeah. He smelled of Aqua Velva.

211
00:10:00,038 --> 00:10:01,080
Aqua Velva.

212
00:10:01,206 --> 00:10:05,502
I don't think there's anything uncommon
about that around here, though.

213
00:10:15,094 --> 00:10:16,137
He's not here.

214
00:10:18,556 --> 00:10:19,599
Teresa?

215
00:10:20,517 --> 00:10:21,684
Teresa Lisbon?

216
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:23,603
T.J. Mullins.

217
00:10:23,728 --> 00:10:25,605
- Hey, T.J.
- Hey, how's it going?

218
00:10:25,730 --> 00:10:27,607
Oh, my God.
T.J. Mullins.

219
00:10:27,732 --> 00:10:28,775
- I heard.
- Yeah.

220
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:30,527
- Yeah, nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you, too.

221
00:10:30,652 --> 00:10:32,320
This one used to babysit me.

222
00:10:32,654 --> 00:10:33,738
- Really?
- Yeah.

223
00:10:34,155 --> 00:10:36,074
Remember when you sat for me
and I locked you out of the house

224
00:10:36,199 --> 00:10:38,785
and you threw a brick
through the basement window to get back in?

225
00:10:38,993 --> 00:10:40,328
And it was completely my fault

226
00:10:40,828 --> 00:10:42,205
and you paid my dad
for the window.

227
00:10:42,330 --> 00:10:44,874
You were such a straight arrow, Teresa.

228
00:10:45,291 --> 00:10:47,794
Thanks. Uh, you know
we're looking for Jimmy.

229
00:10:47,961 --> 00:10:50,213
- Have you seen him?
- No, I haven't seen him.

230
00:10:51,881 --> 00:10:54,634
- Have you talked to him?
- No, no. Definitely not.

231
00:10:54,884 --> 00:10:58,388
T.J., you seem like a very nice kid
but you're a terrible liar.

232
00:10:58,805 --> 00:11:01,140
I'd bet we will find a call
from Jimmy on here.

233
00:11:01,266 --> 00:11:02,350
Hey, where'd you get that?

234
00:11:03,017 --> 00:11:04,769
- That's my phone.
- Yes, it is.

235
00:11:05,270 --> 00:11:06,312
He called this morning.

236
00:11:06,604 --> 00:11:08,398
Look, we need to find him.
It's important.

237
00:11:10,441 --> 00:11:12,735
I said I wouldn't tell
if anybody came looking.

238
00:11:13,069 --> 00:11:14,529
Uh, it's a family emergency.

239
00:11:17,824 --> 00:11:18,866
Yeah.

240
00:11:20,827 --> 00:11:22,370
He said something
about going fishing.

241
00:11:25,290 --> 00:11:27,083
- That's all I got.
- Thanks.

242
00:11:28,585 --> 00:11:29,627
Your mom called.

243
00:11:30,253 --> 00:11:31,379
Should probably call her back.

244
00:11:31,921 --> 00:11:32,964
See you, TJ.

245
00:11:47,770 --> 00:11:48,813
Hey.

246
00:11:49,939 --> 00:11:51,816
Sis, what are you
doing here?

247
00:11:52,150 --> 00:11:54,110
There's a warrant out
for your arrest.

248
00:11:54,444 --> 00:11:56,279
You're wanted for questioning
by the U.S. attorney

249
00:11:56,404 --> 00:11:57,447
and you ran away.

250
00:11:57,780 --> 00:11:59,991
Like do you have any idea
how much trouble you're in?

251
00:12:01,075 --> 00:12:02,118
Catch anything?

252
00:12:05,413 --> 00:12:07,206
No. Your boyfriend?

253
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:09,167
- Yeah. Patrick.
- Hi.

254
00:12:09,667 --> 00:12:10,710
I wanna help.

255
00:12:11,544 --> 00:12:13,671
- Did I ask for your help?
- No, but you're my brother.

256
00:12:13,796 --> 00:12:14,839
Yeah, I'm your brother.

257
00:12:14,964 --> 00:12:16,007
You know, it's funny
how I'm only your brother

258
00:12:16,132 --> 00:12:17,300
when you think I messed up.

259
00:12:17,675 --> 00:12:19,010
Look, talking to an FBI agent

260
00:12:19,135 --> 00:12:20,762
is not a great idea
for me right now.

261
00:12:20,887 --> 00:12:23,097
Talking to the feds is
gonna get me in hot water

262
00:12:23,222 --> 00:12:24,390
with a very dangerous guy.

263
00:12:24,515 --> 00:12:26,643
Who? The guy who came
looking for you at the house?

264
00:12:26,976 --> 00:12:28,019
Someone was at the house?

265
00:12:28,144 --> 00:12:29,604
Yeah, somebody
broke into the house.

266
00:12:30,188 --> 00:12:32,649
Stan says he thinks he was there
to collect a gambling debt.

267
00:12:33,274 --> 00:12:35,318
Or maybe it has something to do
with what happened in Dallas.

268
00:12:35,443 --> 00:12:37,028
- What is it?
- You talked to Stan?

269
00:12:37,236 --> 00:12:38,321
Yeah. Earlier today.

270
00:12:38,946 --> 00:12:39,989
Is he right?

271
00:12:40,198 --> 00:12:41,366
Was the guy
collecting a debt?

272
00:12:42,992 --> 00:12:44,661
I don't know. Maybe.

273
00:12:44,786 --> 00:12:46,287
You're gambling again?
Are you playing poker?

274
00:12:46,412 --> 00:12:48,164
Would you back off me
for like one minute?

275
00:12:48,331 --> 00:12:51,876
Uh, do you mind if I have a little talk
with your brother alone?

276
00:12:56,756 --> 00:13:00,426
No offense, but "sister's boyfriend"
isn't exactly a position of authority to me.

277
00:13:01,761 --> 00:13:02,887
Let me offer you a deal.

278
00:13:04,263 --> 00:13:06,265
You come back to Texas
with your sister and me

279
00:13:06,391 --> 00:13:08,142
and you'll never
have to testify.

280
00:13:08,601 --> 00:13:11,062
And no one will ever know
that you helped us.

281
00:13:12,605 --> 00:13:13,690
How do you swing that?

282
00:13:14,023 --> 00:13:17,276
We'll catch the killer in a way that
your testimony will be unnecessary.

283
00:13:17,819 --> 00:13:18,861
Just like that?

284
00:13:18,986 --> 00:13:20,738
Well, I skipped a few steps
in the middle, but yeah.

285
00:13:24,867 --> 00:13:26,035
I don't even know you, man.

286
00:13:26,285 --> 00:13:27,328
Why should I trust you?

287
00:13:27,453 --> 00:13:29,038
Because I haven't told your sister
about the man in the house

288
00:13:29,163 --> 00:13:30,415
and why he was really there.

289
00:13:30,707 --> 00:13:31,791
I know he's not from Dallas

290
00:13:31,916 --> 00:13:34,877
and I don't think that he was there
to collect on a gambling debt.

291
00:13:37,839 --> 00:13:38,881
Do I have to go on?

292
00:13:40,341 --> 00:13:41,384
No.

293
00:13:42,677 --> 00:13:45,596
Look, I... I don't like
keeping secrets from Teresa.

294
00:13:46,556 --> 00:13:47,598
I care about her.

295
00:13:49,684 --> 00:13:52,478
And I care about the people
that she cares about.

296
00:13:53,020 --> 00:13:55,523
You come back to Texas
and you'll be fine. I promise.

297
00:14:03,614 --> 00:14:04,657
We're good.

298
00:14:21,280 --> 00:14:23,532
- This is where you work?
- It is, yeah.

299
00:14:24,199 --> 00:14:25,242
Fancy.

300
00:14:25,492 --> 00:14:27,244
Step up from the fryer
at Casper's.

301
00:14:27,953 --> 00:14:29,705
It's probably better
for your face, too.

302
00:14:31,290 --> 00:14:33,208
Hi. I'm Jimmy Lisbon.

303
00:14:33,917 --> 00:14:35,836
- Can I help you?
- Jimmy, come on. Let's go.

304
00:14:37,171 --> 00:14:38,213
Later.

305
00:14:43,886 --> 00:14:45,053
- Get in.
- Okay.

306
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:53,770
You're recording me? You
gonna read me my rights first?

307
00:14:53,896 --> 00:14:56,440
I have to put this on record.
It's for your own good.

308
00:14:58,108 --> 00:14:59,151
What were you doing in Dallas

309
00:14:59,276 --> 00:15:00,944
the night Nathan Barnes
was killed?

310
00:15:01,361 --> 00:15:03,363
- You're gonna be mad.
- Jimmy.

311
00:15:03,697 --> 00:15:06,033
Okay, but I don't wanna
hear about it.

312
00:15:07,826 --> 00:15:10,287
I was at a poker game
at the Wrightwood Hotel.

313
00:15:10,412 --> 00:15:11,955
You drove to Dallas
for a poker game?

314
00:15:12,289 --> 00:15:14,208
It's three hours
from Oklahoma City.

315
00:15:14,416 --> 00:15:16,001
You'd drive three hours
for a good game.

316
00:15:16,126 --> 00:15:17,169
No, I wouldn't.

317
00:15:17,294 --> 00:15:20,130
It must've been my other big sister
who taught me how to play cards.

318
00:15:21,381 --> 00:15:22,591
Was the victim at the game?

319
00:15:23,342 --> 00:15:24,927
Yeah. Nathan was there.

320
00:15:25,886 --> 00:15:26,929
We got to talking.

321
00:15:27,054 --> 00:15:28,764
He said he had some
electrical work needed done.

322
00:15:28,889 --> 00:15:31,350
I gave him my card
said I was an electrician.

323
00:15:31,558 --> 00:15:33,810
- Did you see him get killed?
- No way.

324
00:15:35,020 --> 00:15:36,980
- Do you know who did it?
- No.

325
00:15:37,356 --> 00:15:39,233
- Jimmy.
- T, look...

326
00:15:40,817 --> 00:15:43,111
What happens is
I... I go to the Wrightwood, okay?

327
00:15:43,237 --> 00:15:44,696
"And Nathan is there."

328
00:15:44,821 --> 00:15:47,491
"I know him and a friend of his
named Charlie McInnis."

329
00:15:47,658 --> 00:15:48,700
"He's another law clerk."

330
00:15:49,034 --> 00:15:51,662
"They're the only ones I know...
by name, at least."

331
00:15:51,870 --> 00:15:53,872
Do you remember anybody else
who was there?

332
00:15:55,290 --> 00:15:58,502
A woman named Vicki, I think.

333
00:15:58,877 --> 00:16:00,254
Met a dude named Ben.

334
00:16:00,504 --> 00:16:02,839
You said there was somebody
there that you were afraid of.

335
00:16:03,215 --> 00:16:05,008
Don't tell me
you can't remember his name.

336
00:16:10,264 --> 00:16:13,308
The game's run by a guy
named George Holiday.

337
00:16:15,185 --> 00:16:16,937
George Holiday, 50 years old.

338
00:16:17,437 --> 00:16:19,356
He's a major player
in the Dallas organized-crime world.

339
00:16:19,606 --> 00:16:21,525
Union kickbacks, sex trade, drugs

340
00:16:21,650 --> 00:16:23,360
suspected of a few hits
in the '90s

341
00:16:23,485 --> 00:16:24,653
before he moved
into management.

342
00:16:25,404 --> 00:16:28,115
Mobster in cowboy boots
and a big-time gambler.

343
00:16:28,323 --> 00:16:30,242
Nathan Barnes was in a ton of debt
to Holiday.

344
00:16:30,492 --> 00:16:33,954
- How much?
- $140,000, $150,000.

345
00:16:34,162 --> 00:16:36,456
He was a chatty drunk
after a few gin and tonics.

346
00:16:37,124 --> 00:16:38,166
So, there you go.

347
00:16:38,583 --> 00:16:39,626
Have fun catching him.

348
00:16:39,751 --> 00:16:42,254
- I'm not sure Holiday's our guy.
- Why not?

349
00:16:42,587 --> 00:16:44,423
It's hard to get money
out of a dead man.

350
00:16:44,756 --> 00:16:47,092
The killer is almost certainly
a part of that poker game.

351
00:16:47,217 --> 00:16:48,427
We need to get in on that.

352
00:16:48,593 --> 00:16:50,220
Forget it.
Took me weeks.

353
00:16:50,554 --> 00:16:53,223
I had to charm Holiday
with my mad poker skills.

354
00:16:53,432 --> 00:16:54,725
Let us take care of it.

355
00:16:54,850 --> 00:16:55,892
How do we find him?

356
00:16:56,018 --> 00:16:58,979
He's a silent partner at an upscale sports
bar in Dallas called Donovan's.

357
00:16:59,980 --> 00:17:04,026
I just had a contentious phone call
with US Attorney Sandoval.

358
00:17:04,318 --> 00:17:07,279
Her office was alerted by TSA
about your brother's flight.

359
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:10,324
- She asked that we hand him over.
- Whoa.

360
00:17:10,449 --> 00:17:11,950
I mean, you said that
I wouldn't have to do this.

361
00:17:12,117 --> 00:17:13,994
Well, you won't... just yet.

362
00:17:14,328 --> 00:17:15,996
I told her that
we caught a break in the case.

363
00:17:16,413 --> 00:17:19,791
She wasn't happy, but she agreed
to let us follow it for 72 hours.

364
00:17:20,167 --> 00:17:23,587
Now, if we find a suspect in
that time, the collar is hers.

365
00:17:24,379 --> 00:17:27,632
If we don't, then we need
to rethink our strategy.

366
00:17:27,966 --> 00:17:30,844
Uh, Cho and I need
to make friends with a mobster.

367
00:17:31,303 --> 00:17:32,554
We're gonna need some cash.

368
00:17:33,889 --> 00:17:34,931
I'll see what I can do.

369
00:17:37,934 --> 00:17:40,228
Jane, that guy who attacked you
in Chicago?

370
00:17:40,354 --> 00:17:41,396
Mm-hmm?

371
00:17:41,521 --> 00:17:42,564
I found someone who fit
the description you gave.

372
00:17:43,648 --> 00:17:46,693
Name's Delfino.
Low-level thug. It's odd, though.

373
00:17:46,818 --> 00:17:48,070
Lisbon said he was after Jimmy

374
00:17:48,195 --> 00:17:50,614
but I can't find any connection
between the two.

375
00:17:51,114 --> 00:17:52,866
Delfino's Chicago, born-and-bred.

376
00:17:52,991 --> 00:17:54,701
No connection
to Oklahoma city or Dallas.

377
00:17:55,202 --> 00:17:56,244
If he was after Jimmy

378
00:17:57,079 --> 00:17:58,205
I don't know
who he was working for.

379
00:17:59,081 --> 00:18:00,165
Want the locals to pick him up?

380
00:18:00,999 --> 00:18:03,752
No. Uh, let's sit on this
and don't tell anyone, okay?

381
00:18:03,877 --> 00:18:05,128
Sure thing.

382
00:18:15,847 --> 00:18:16,890
Holiday.

383
00:18:17,474 --> 00:18:18,809
- They're gonna run it.
- They're gonna pass.

384
00:18:18,934 --> 00:18:21,603
Okay, let's put it up there.
Let's see, shall we?

385
00:18:21,812 --> 00:18:23,021
Come on, now.

386
00:18:23,647 --> 00:18:25,816
- Here we are. $60.
- You're on.

387
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:27,984
Run it. Run it.

388
00:18:31,279 --> 00:18:33,281
- Yes.
- Oh.

389
00:18:33,657 --> 00:18:36,118
- I do love taking your money.
- Well, I'll have my revenge.

390
00:18:36,243 --> 00:18:37,285
Mm-hmm.

391
00:18:38,662 --> 00:18:39,704
- Another?
- Yeah.

392
00:18:39,830 --> 00:18:42,791
Uh, bartender, two more drinks.
Oh, drinks on me.

393
00:18:42,999 --> 00:18:44,042
Sir, you want a drink?

394
00:18:44,709 --> 00:18:45,752
I'm buying.

395
00:18:46,169 --> 00:18:47,754
- I buy my own drinks, thanks.
- Smart man.

396
00:18:47,879 --> 00:18:49,840
Never put yourself
in another person's debt.

397
00:18:50,340 --> 00:18:52,676
Uh, let's make this a little
more interesting, shall we?

398
00:18:52,801 --> 00:18:55,595
A thousand says next drive
ties the game.

399
00:18:56,054 --> 00:18:59,099
- That's too much for me.
- Nah. $1,000. Come on.

400
00:18:59,266 --> 00:19:01,768
$1,000.
Anyone want in?

401
00:19:01,977 --> 00:19:03,019
Money on the bar.

402
00:19:03,311 --> 00:19:04,729
Do you know anything
about football?

403
00:19:05,105 --> 00:19:06,898
Why don't you take the bet
and find out?

404
00:19:10,193 --> 00:19:11,945
You ought to be more careful
with your money...

405
00:19:14,739 --> 00:19:15,782
and your mouth.

406
00:19:17,868 --> 00:19:21,371
Thank you...
For the advice.

407
00:19:24,207 --> 00:19:25,750
Goodness, you look delicious.

408
00:19:25,917 --> 00:19:27,669
Eh, fishing with the wrong bait.

409
00:19:34,968 --> 00:19:36,011
Charlie McInnis?

410
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:38,180
I'm Agent Michelle Vega.

411
00:19:38,430 --> 00:19:41,475
I'd like to talk to you about the murder
of judge Barnes' son, Nathan.

412
00:19:41,808 --> 00:19:42,851
Sure.

413
00:19:43,435 --> 00:19:44,644
Yeah, terrible what happened.

414
00:19:46,021 --> 00:19:48,982
Um, Heidi Pendleton.
This is my fiancée.

415
00:19:49,357 --> 00:19:50,692
We work with Judge Barnes.

416
00:19:50,817 --> 00:19:51,860
Hi.

417
00:19:52,027 --> 00:19:54,529
Nathan was an amazing guy.

418
00:19:54,654 --> 00:19:58,867
- I... um, I'm sorry.
- It's okay.

419
00:19:59,159 --> 00:20:02,496
Uh... It seems so senseless
what happened.

420
00:20:04,539 --> 00:20:06,833
I helped Nathan with some
of his domestic-abuse cases.

421
00:20:06,958 --> 00:20:08,335
We became friends through that.

422
00:20:08,919 --> 00:20:11,254
Nathan was at a poker game
the night he got killed.

423
00:20:11,922 --> 00:20:13,465
You were there, too
weren't you, Mr. McInnis?

424
00:20:13,757 --> 00:20:14,799
Yes.

425
00:20:14,925 --> 00:20:17,594
- So you know George Holiday.
- Yeah, but just from the game.

426
00:20:18,053 --> 00:20:19,304
Who else did you know
at the game?

427
00:20:19,846 --> 00:20:22,599
Um... Nathan, obviously

428
00:20:23,892 --> 00:20:25,894
a kid named
Jimmy Lisbon

429
00:20:26,019 --> 00:20:27,479
uh, there was a woman
named Vicki Shell

430
00:20:27,854 --> 00:20:28,897
and Benjamin Bennett.

431
00:20:29,022 --> 00:20:32,150
- You played poker with Bennett?
- Yeah, it was nothing.

432
00:20:33,276 --> 00:20:34,653
What do you know
about Benjamin Bennett?

433
00:20:35,654 --> 00:20:39,032
Judge Barnes ruled against him
in a patent case a few months back.

434
00:20:39,824 --> 00:20:41,284
He was ticked off.

435
00:20:41,451 --> 00:20:42,994
There was a lot of money involved.

436
00:20:43,161 --> 00:20:44,704
That's how we know him.
You know, through the paperwork.

437
00:20:44,913 --> 00:20:47,749
And the poker game?
Isn't that a conflict of interest?

438
00:20:48,291 --> 00:20:49,793
I mean, I never discussed
the case with him.

439
00:20:50,210 --> 00:20:51,253
But someone did?

440
00:20:52,128 --> 00:20:54,714
Well, Bennett was working Nathan
about it

441
00:20:54,881 --> 00:20:57,884
wanted to get his mom
to revisit the ruling.

442
00:20:58,134 --> 00:21:01,930
Nathan said no, of course
but, uh, Bennett wouldn't let it go.

443
00:21:08,061 --> 00:21:10,272
So, there were six players
at the poker game.

444
00:21:10,647 --> 00:21:11,690
George Holiday.

445
00:21:11,815 --> 00:21:14,484
Nathan was in debt to Holiday
for 140 grand.

446
00:21:14,609 --> 00:21:16,444
That's a big chip
for Holiday to play.

447
00:21:16,570 --> 00:21:17,612
Charlie McInnis?

448
00:21:17,946 --> 00:21:19,948
"He lost big that night.
Not a good night for him."

449
00:21:20,323 --> 00:21:21,950
"Benjamin Bennett
goes by Benben."

450
00:21:22,117 --> 00:21:25,370
Former college basketball star
trying to make it as an entrepreneur.

451
00:21:25,662 --> 00:21:28,373
The victim's mother ruled
against him in a patent case.

452
00:21:28,540 --> 00:21:32,127
"Vicki Shell, avid cyclist and CEO
of a Dallas bicycle manufacturer."

453
00:21:32,294 --> 00:21:34,296
"According to Jimmy
she had an eye for the victim."

454
00:21:34,421 --> 00:21:35,839
You're sure one of them
killed Nathan?

455
00:21:35,964 --> 00:21:37,007
Well, it seems likely.

456
00:21:37,132 --> 00:21:39,009
We won't know for sure
until we get into the game.

457
00:21:39,175 --> 00:21:40,635
Well, how'd it go with Holiday?
You in?

458
00:21:40,760 --> 00:21:41,803
Not yet.

459
00:21:42,596 --> 00:21:44,306
He needs a different kind
of motivation.

460
00:21:44,681 --> 00:21:45,724
What kind?

461
00:22:00,947 --> 00:22:02,324
Scotch on the rocks, please.

462
00:22:15,420 --> 00:22:18,840
- On the house.
- Thank you, kind stranger.

463
00:22:20,759 --> 00:22:23,928
- George, please.
- Teresa.

464
00:22:24,095 --> 00:22:25,138
Teresa.

465
00:22:26,556 --> 00:22:28,099
So, what's your story, Teresa?

466
00:22:42,697 --> 00:22:44,324
I gotta tell you something, buddy.

467
00:22:44,616 --> 00:22:46,201
You got a much better sense
about women

468
00:22:46,326 --> 00:22:47,577
than you do about football.

469
00:22:47,827 --> 00:22:49,120
Well, it's just money.

470
00:22:50,830 --> 00:22:52,707
You really mean that
you've never been broke.

471
00:22:53,416 --> 00:22:54,501
Well, what's the point
of having money

472
00:22:54,626 --> 00:22:56,586
if you can't have fun with it, right?

473
00:22:57,420 --> 00:23:00,507
Betting on sports is fun
but, uh, there's no skill in it.

474
00:23:00,882 --> 00:23:02,300
Gets boring after a while.

475
00:23:02,884 --> 00:23:03,927
You play cards?

476
00:23:04,219 --> 00:23:05,804
He's terrible at poker.

477
00:23:05,970 --> 00:23:07,639
- Stop it. You're drunk.
- You're drunk.

478
00:23:07,764 --> 00:23:08,807
I'm good at cards.

479
00:23:08,932 --> 00:23:11,351
He lost $27,000
in one poker game

480
00:23:11,518 --> 00:23:12,811
and then he told me
it was fun.

481
00:23:12,936 --> 00:23:15,397
It was fun.
It was fun... for a while.

482
00:23:15,522 --> 00:23:17,148
I mean here's the thing with cards.

483
00:23:18,233 --> 00:23:21,986
It's like a showdown
in the Wild West... kill or be killed.

484
00:23:22,404 --> 00:23:23,571
I mean, who doesn't love that?

485
00:23:26,324 --> 00:23:27,701
It's nothing like that at all.

486
00:23:30,245 --> 00:23:32,497
You know, I might
know of a game... big one.

487
00:23:33,331 --> 00:23:35,625
Five grand buy-in. Is that
something that might interest you?

488
00:23:37,502 --> 00:23:39,587
Deal me in there, partner.

489
00:23:43,940 --> 00:23:44,982
Jane's in the game.

490
00:23:45,149 --> 00:23:46,859
- The Wrightwood Hotel?
- Presidential suite.

491
00:23:46,984 --> 00:23:48,903
We're gonna need surveillance
cameras all over that place.

492
00:23:49,070 --> 00:23:50,112
You got a plan
for getting them in?

493
00:23:51,948 --> 00:23:53,574
Yeah, I believe we do.

494
00:23:57,995 --> 00:23:59,080
The wedding's next year

495
00:23:59,205 --> 00:24:01,332
and we were thinking
about holding it here at the Wrightwood.

496
00:24:01,457 --> 00:24:03,543
And then we were shopping
and thought, "What they hey?"

497
00:24:03,668 --> 00:24:04,961
"Let's check it out."

498
00:24:05,294 --> 00:24:06,879
- It's nice, huh?
- I guess.

499
00:24:07,046 --> 00:24:09,507
Well, we actually have an array
of all-inclusive wedding packages.

500
00:24:09,632 --> 00:24:10,842
We just wanna see the room.

501
00:24:11,133 --> 00:24:12,635
Oh. Of course.

502
00:24:13,928 --> 00:24:14,971
This here.

503
00:24:18,766 --> 00:24:19,809
And here we go.

504
00:24:19,934 --> 00:24:21,644
And the table is set up
for an event tonight.

505
00:24:22,228 --> 00:24:23,271
Wow.

506
00:24:23,396 --> 00:24:25,106
This is really nice.
I think this could work, honey.

507
00:24:25,231 --> 00:24:27,567
You think. Hmm?
Do you care what I think?

508
00:24:28,025 --> 00:24:29,819
- You don't like it.
- Does it matter?

509
00:24:30,027 --> 00:24:31,487
You only care
about what your mother likes.

510
00:24:32,029 --> 00:24:33,364
Don't talk about my mother.

511
00:24:33,489 --> 00:24:36,033
Oh, I think we need
to talk about your mother.

512
00:24:36,158 --> 00:24:37,326
No, I think you need
to calm down.

513
00:24:37,451 --> 00:24:38,744
Do not tell me to calm down.

514
00:24:38,870 --> 00:24:41,289
Seriously, you're embarrassing me.

515
00:24:49,422 --> 00:24:51,716
I'll leave you to talk things over.

516
00:24:52,049 --> 00:24:53,467
I'll be at the front desk
if you need me.

517
00:25:01,726 --> 00:25:03,936
Camera in the corner
camera on the counter

518
00:25:04,061 --> 00:25:05,438
camera on the thermostat.

519
00:25:05,605 --> 00:25:07,023
I didn't know you were
gonna flip to Spanish.

520
00:25:07,189 --> 00:25:09,442
Kind of a spur-of-the-moment thing.
Did you understand?

521
00:25:09,609 --> 00:25:11,027
Something about
ripping my head off?

522
00:25:11,527 --> 00:25:12,570
You've been studying.

523
00:25:12,778 --> 00:25:13,821
Hand me the wrench.

524
00:25:14,280 --> 00:25:15,323
Thanks.

525
00:25:31,130 --> 00:25:32,214
You don't see it at all.

526
00:25:33,966 --> 00:25:35,009
Thanks.

527
00:25:35,927 --> 00:25:36,969
How's the toilet?

528
00:25:37,345 --> 00:25:38,387
Busted.

529
00:25:39,096 --> 00:25:40,139
Excellent. Let's go.

530
00:25:50,107 --> 00:25:51,150
Hello?

531
00:25:51,651 --> 00:25:53,152
Teresa, I didn't know who else to call.

532
00:25:53,444 --> 00:25:57,114
- Karen? What's wrong?
- Stan got beat up.

533
00:25:57,573 --> 00:25:58,991
Oh, my God.
Is he okay?

534
00:25:59,617 --> 00:26:01,243
He said it was an accident at work.

535
00:26:02,787 --> 00:26:03,829
I don't believe him.

536
00:26:04,163 --> 00:26:05,206
"Leave it alone, T."

537
00:26:05,331 --> 00:26:07,041
No. Your wife
is scared to death.

538
00:26:07,208 --> 00:26:09,502
- Who did this?
- "A couple of guys got drunk"

539
00:26:09,627 --> 00:26:11,170
"and were looking
for trouble, all right?"

540
00:26:11,337 --> 00:26:14,298
That's not what you told Karen.
Uh, why are you lying to me?

541
00:26:14,590 --> 00:26:15,633
"I'm not."

542
00:26:15,883 --> 00:26:17,927
Look, I know crap
when I hear it, Stan.

543
00:26:19,261 --> 00:26:21,639
I am gonna kill Jimmy
for getting you involved in this.

544
00:26:22,014 --> 00:26:24,642
"Just stay out of it.
Please?"

545
00:26:25,101 --> 00:26:26,143
I'll talk to you later.

546
00:26:27,478 --> 00:26:28,521
Gotta catch that.

547
00:26:35,277 --> 00:26:36,529
What's going on with Stan?

548
00:26:37,238 --> 00:26:38,572
What? Nothing.

549
00:26:39,323 --> 00:26:41,701
That's what Jane was talking
to you about at the lake.

550
00:26:42,410 --> 00:26:43,911
Why you agreed
to come out here.

551
00:26:44,662 --> 00:26:46,288
You're hiding something
about Stan.

552
00:26:49,166 --> 00:26:53,421
Jimmy... come on.
Tell me what's going on.

553
00:27:00,636 --> 00:27:02,888
Stan had a couple bad breaks
in his business.

554
00:27:04,598 --> 00:27:06,225
Karen's last pregnancy
was tough.

555
00:27:06,350 --> 00:27:07,727
He got behind on his bills.

556
00:27:09,812 --> 00:27:11,397
He owes money
to the wrong people.

557
00:27:11,689 --> 00:27:13,774
A loan shark.
What's he in for?

558
00:27:13,899 --> 00:27:14,984
Over 30 grand.

559
00:27:15,151 --> 00:27:17,236
Thirty? God.

560
00:27:19,780 --> 00:27:22,033
The man that attacked Jane...
he wasn't looking for you.

561
00:27:22,158 --> 00:27:23,451
He was there for Stan.

562
00:27:25,161 --> 00:27:26,454
Why'd you cover for him?

563
00:27:27,079 --> 00:27:30,332
Stan, he's... he's working
so hard to be good.

564
00:27:31,167 --> 00:27:32,668
Just wanted you to be proud of him.

565
00:27:32,960 --> 00:27:34,045
I am proud of him.

566
00:27:35,046 --> 00:27:36,088
I'm proud of all of you.

567
00:27:36,505 --> 00:27:37,548
Really?

568
00:27:38,591 --> 00:27:41,010
Did you call me when
I got my electrician's license?

569
00:27:42,678 --> 00:27:45,806
You only call to yell at me
just like always.

570
00:27:47,099 --> 00:27:50,853
Look, I know I was tough on you
when you were a kid, but come on.

571
00:27:50,978 --> 00:27:52,521
You know what mom and dad were like.

572
00:27:52,855 --> 00:27:56,442
Somebody had to be responsible
and somebody had to be in charge.

573
00:27:56,650 --> 00:27:58,527
Yeah?
You were in charge.

574
00:28:00,780 --> 00:28:01,822
Then you left.

575
00:28:13,751 --> 00:28:16,003
- So, Jimmy's gonna be part of this?
- Yeah. Has to be.

576
00:28:16,128 --> 00:28:17,630
- He's gonna play in the game?
- I need him there.

577
00:28:17,755 --> 00:28:18,798
Well, then I'm gonna be there.

578
00:28:18,923 --> 00:28:20,174
He'll be safe.
We'll have eyes on them.

579
00:28:20,299 --> 00:28:21,926
He's my little brother.
I'm gonna be there.

580
00:28:22,343 --> 00:28:23,385
Yeah, of course.

581
00:28:23,844 --> 00:28:24,887
How's it gonna go?

582
00:28:25,096 --> 00:28:26,597
Jimmy's gonna make contact
with all the suspects.

583
00:28:26,722 --> 00:28:28,015
"Holiday's sending the invitation."

584
00:28:28,182 --> 00:28:29,433
"Jimmy's gonna make sure
they show up."

585
00:28:31,685 --> 00:28:33,229
- McInnis.
- Charlie, hey.

586
00:28:33,479 --> 00:28:34,647
It's Jimmy from the poker game.

587
00:28:34,772 --> 00:28:37,316
Well, hello, Jimmy from the poker game.

588
00:28:37,441 --> 00:28:38,484
What's going on?

589
00:28:38,609 --> 00:28:40,361
Did you get
George Holiday's invitation?

590
00:28:40,945 --> 00:28:41,987
"There's a game tonight."

591
00:28:42,488 --> 00:28:43,948
"And then he will use the word"

592
00:28:44,073 --> 00:28:45,908
"that makes every poker player
smell blood."

593
00:28:46,075 --> 00:28:48,119
I'm telling you, Ben.
This guy's a whale. Okay?

594
00:28:48,244 --> 00:28:49,453
One of my friends played with him.

595
00:28:49,829 --> 00:28:51,956
This guy dropped like $20,000
in one night.

596
00:28:52,665 --> 00:28:53,707
For real?

597
00:28:56,919 --> 00:28:58,212
He's a terrible player.

598
00:28:59,130 --> 00:29:00,881
Doesn't care
if he wins or loses.

599
00:29:01,298 --> 00:29:02,424
Just wants action.

600
00:29:03,300 --> 00:29:04,343
We'll clean him out.

601
00:29:09,515 --> 00:29:10,891
Where are we with the surveillance?

602
00:29:11,642 --> 00:29:14,395
Cameras coming online...
Now.

603
00:29:14,854 --> 00:29:17,982
Holiday, Jimmy Lisbon
Charlie McInnis, Vicki Shell

604
00:29:18,107 --> 00:29:19,650
and Benben are in the room.

605
00:29:19,942 --> 00:29:21,861
All right. Tell Jane
and Lisbon we're ready.

606
00:29:25,072 --> 00:29:26,115
Yep.

607
00:29:26,615 --> 00:29:28,200
That was Wylie.
They're all set.

608
00:29:30,244 --> 00:29:31,287
Hey.

609
00:29:31,579 --> 00:29:32,872
I'm sorry.
Um, yeah, I'm ready.

610
00:29:33,581 --> 00:29:34,623
Let's go.

611
00:29:35,624 --> 00:29:38,544
Your brothers don't hate you, you know.

612
00:29:39,670 --> 00:29:41,505
- Yeah, they do.
- No, they don't.

613
00:29:42,464 --> 00:29:44,049
Jimmy's right.
I left.

614
00:29:44,633 --> 00:29:48,554
After my mom died
I was the parent, and I left.

615
00:29:48,929 --> 00:29:51,140
Well, you felt trapped.
Of course you did.

616
00:29:51,265 --> 00:29:54,643
Now Stan's life is a mess
Jimmy's got a gambling problem

617
00:29:54,768 --> 00:29:56,437
and God only knows
what Tommy's up to.

618
00:29:56,562 --> 00:29:58,439
Yeah, sure, look
they've got their problems.

619
00:29:58,564 --> 00:29:59,940
But they're good people.

620
00:30:01,358 --> 00:30:02,401
And they wouldn't even be here

621
00:30:02,526 --> 00:30:04,778
if you hadn't loved and protected them
when they were kids.

622
00:30:06,030 --> 00:30:09,074
You're uncomfortable around them
because you feel guilt.

623
00:30:09,491 --> 00:30:10,826
I understand that.

624
00:30:12,286 --> 00:30:14,622
But you need to know
they're not mad at you.

625
00:30:15,539 --> 00:30:16,582
They're not.

626
00:30:17,499 --> 00:30:18,626
They just miss you.

627
00:30:22,588 --> 00:30:24,465
You knew exactly
what was going on

628
00:30:24,882 --> 00:30:26,926
with Stan and Jimmy
and the guy at the house.

629
00:30:27,051 --> 00:30:30,221
You figured it out
and you didn't say a word to me.

630
00:30:31,055 --> 00:30:34,141
Well...
It's not my business.

631
00:30:35,851 --> 00:30:36,894
Thank you.

632
00:30:38,812 --> 00:30:39,855
All right, let's go.

633
00:30:39,980 --> 00:30:42,066
- We've got a game to get to.
- Absolutely.

634
00:30:46,737 --> 00:30:48,656
- Welcome.
- You remember Teresa?

635
00:30:49,240 --> 00:30:50,574
I'm just here to watch.

636
00:30:51,075 --> 00:30:52,534
Make yourself at home, darling.

637
00:30:56,789 --> 00:30:58,832
Take any more of my money
you're gonna have to buy me dinner.

638
00:31:00,084 --> 00:31:01,126
We'll see.

639
00:31:01,585 --> 00:31:03,379
"That was a bad beat
last week, Charlie."

640
00:31:03,504 --> 00:31:05,589
You don't have to do anything
other than play poker.

641
00:31:05,714 --> 00:31:07,549
Focus on the game.
Let me do the work.

642
00:31:07,841 --> 00:31:10,010
- What work, exactly?
- You'll see.

643
00:31:10,386 --> 00:31:11,804
First, another drink.

644
00:31:15,557 --> 00:31:16,600
Toilet's busted.

645
00:31:18,060 --> 00:31:19,645
- Plugged?
- It's not flushing.

646
00:31:21,105 --> 00:31:22,147
Don't go in there.

647
00:31:24,400 --> 00:31:25,985
All right, so what do you guys wanna do?

648
00:31:26,110 --> 00:31:27,695
You wanna pull up stakes
and take it to another room?

649
00:31:27,861 --> 00:31:30,864
We... we're gonna relocate
just because there's a plumbing snafu?

650
00:31:31,073 --> 00:31:33,158
I mean, I... I... I didn't come here
to go to the bathroom.

651
00:31:33,284 --> 00:31:35,452
I came here to play poker.
Let's just play poker.

652
00:31:35,661 --> 00:31:37,079
Man wants to play cards.

653
00:31:37,371 --> 00:31:38,706
- So be it.
- Okay with me

654
00:31:38,831 --> 00:31:39,873
All right.

655
00:31:39,999 --> 00:31:44,962
There is a washroom down
at the end of the hall by the health club.

656
00:31:45,587 --> 00:31:48,382
- All right.
- Take a walk or hold your water.

657
00:31:49,216 --> 00:31:51,260
Patrick Jane.
That's my girlfriend, Teresa.

658
00:31:51,468 --> 00:31:53,679
I'm just here to watch
and enjoy the open bar.

659
00:31:54,013 --> 00:31:57,057
The game is Texas Hold'em.

660
00:31:58,309 --> 00:31:59,351
No limit.

661
00:32:04,315 --> 00:32:05,858
Start off a little slow.

662
00:32:17,369 --> 00:32:18,412
And away we go.

663
00:32:31,008 --> 00:32:33,260
"All right, ante up.
Gotta be on the decline."

664
00:32:34,094 --> 00:32:35,888
- "Yeah."
- So, is Jane cheating?

665
00:32:36,847 --> 00:32:38,515
Yeah, but he isn't playing to win.

666
00:32:38,724 --> 00:32:40,768
He's watching the other players
so he can learn their tells.

667
00:32:41,226 --> 00:32:43,354
Oh, what do we have
on Fourth Street, here?

668
00:32:43,479 --> 00:32:45,147
Subtle behaviors a player makes

669
00:32:45,272 --> 00:32:46,774
when he has a good
or a bad hand.

670
00:32:47,649 --> 00:32:48,817
I know what a tell is.

671
00:32:54,573 --> 00:32:55,616
Nose rub.

672
00:32:56,533 --> 00:32:58,702
Last time she did that
she got a flush.

673
00:32:59,244 --> 00:33:01,372
The nose rub is her tell.

674
00:33:05,709 --> 00:33:06,752
Ha. Told you.

675
00:33:10,506 --> 00:33:11,715
Okay, game on.

676
00:33:18,305 --> 00:33:19,807
Rocking.
He rocks side to side.

677
00:33:26,021 --> 00:33:27,272
Oh! Eyebrow scratch.

678
00:33:35,072 --> 00:33:36,115
Hair scratch.

679
00:33:36,407 --> 00:33:37,449
That's all of them.

680
00:33:38,367 --> 00:33:39,410
Time for phase two.

681
00:33:40,536 --> 00:33:42,162
So, it's back to me, huh?

682
00:33:42,579 --> 00:33:45,040
Well, we all feeling good?
Are we feeling all right there, honey?

683
00:33:45,582 --> 00:33:46,625
I don't know.

684
00:33:47,042 --> 00:33:49,128
There's something disturbing
in this room.

685
00:33:49,253 --> 00:33:52,840
Ah, she's a little sensitive
a little psychic.

686
00:33:53,257 --> 00:33:54,383
- Psychic?
- Almost.

687
00:33:55,217 --> 00:33:58,178
Was somebody
killed here recently?

688
00:33:58,470 --> 00:33:59,513
Oh, my God.

689
00:33:59,638 --> 00:34:03,517
Uh, not in this room, but, yeah
one of our players was killed.

690
00:34:04,476 --> 00:34:06,687
Nate... no.
Uh, Nathan.

691
00:34:06,812 --> 00:34:09,231
- Is... is that his name?
- This is getting a little weird.

692
00:34:09,440 --> 00:34:11,900
Amazing, isn't she?
Uh, it's kind of uncanny.

693
00:34:13,277 --> 00:34:14,319
Yeah.

694
00:34:15,320 --> 00:34:16,530
We're playing poker, aren't we?

695
00:34:18,031 --> 00:34:19,700
- I'm in.
- I'm sorry.

696
00:34:20,325 --> 00:34:21,368
Wait, wait, wait.

697
00:34:21,493 --> 00:34:23,537
- Uh, Th... there's more.
- There is?

698
00:34:23,996 --> 00:34:26,123
I'm feeling a darker presence.

699
00:34:27,332 --> 00:34:28,625
The killer is in this room.

700
00:34:28,792 --> 00:34:31,503
- Oh, come on.
- One of you killed Nathan.

701
00:34:33,172 --> 00:34:35,215
Wait.
Don't touch your cards.

702
00:34:36,675 --> 00:34:39,219
The killer is the one who has the ace.

703
00:34:46,602 --> 00:34:48,562
I think things just got interesting.

704
00:34:53,356 --> 00:34:54,941
She says the killer's
holding an ace.

705
00:34:55,900 --> 00:34:56,943
I'm curious.

706
00:35:21,359 --> 00:35:22,401
It's McInnis.

707
00:35:31,994 --> 00:35:34,038
Looks like daddy's
going to the big house.

708
00:35:42,171 --> 00:35:43,214
Whoops.

709
00:35:43,381 --> 00:35:45,508
Gonna go get myself a drink.

710
00:35:45,883 --> 00:35:47,969
Not so much of a psychic
after all, I guess.

711
00:35:48,594 --> 00:35:49,929
Now, can we play some cards?

712
00:35:50,680 --> 00:35:51,764
So, are we ready to go?

713
00:35:52,348 --> 00:35:53,391
Not yet.

714
00:35:53,516 --> 00:35:55,143
Now Jane makes sure
McInnis wins.

715
00:36:15,413 --> 00:36:18,624
- Ah, take it.
- Oh, look out, daddy.

716
00:36:19,083 --> 00:36:20,126
Lucky guy.

717
00:36:21,377 --> 00:36:23,337
- You're good. You're good.
- Boy, you're hot.

718
00:36:24,172 --> 00:36:26,048
- You're having a good night.
- Mm-hmm.

719
00:36:26,674 --> 00:36:28,885
Okay, I am now
gonna take the long walk

720
00:36:29,510 --> 00:36:30,636
to the little boy's room.

721
00:36:32,221 --> 00:36:34,348
I'm feeling a little warm.
I don't know about anyone else.

722
00:36:35,391 --> 00:36:36,767
Time for a drink.

723
00:36:38,895 --> 00:36:39,937
Or two.

724
00:36:41,606 --> 00:36:42,648
Can I get you something?

725
00:36:43,191 --> 00:36:44,233
What the hell is this?

726
00:36:44,775 --> 00:36:46,527
- What?
- Honey, we're leaving.

727
00:36:47,069 --> 00:36:48,863
- What? Why?
- We're in the middle of a game.

728
00:36:49,030 --> 00:36:50,448
Uh, there's a hidden camera here.

729
00:36:51,199 --> 00:36:52,283
- Are you kidding?
- What?

730
00:36:53,534 --> 00:36:54,577
There.

731
00:36:55,494 --> 00:36:56,537
Camera?

732
00:37:03,252 --> 00:37:04,337
What the hell?

733
00:37:06,464 --> 00:37:07,506
Mr. McInnis.

734
00:37:09,258 --> 00:37:11,093
Agent Kimball Cho, FBI.

735
00:37:11,385 --> 00:37:13,596
- What is this? What's going on?
- We know you killed Nathan Barnes.

736
00:37:13,846 --> 00:37:15,973
What?
That's ridiculous.

737
00:37:16,098 --> 00:37:19,143
Our agents in the room
are telling Holiday it was you.

738
00:37:24,774 --> 00:37:26,484
McInnis has been winning
all night.

739
00:37:27,485 --> 00:37:30,363
He's got someone watching in
another room, feeding him cards.

740
00:37:30,488 --> 00:37:32,031
Oh, geez.

741
00:37:42,124 --> 00:37:43,584
Now, Barnes owed Holiday
a lot of money.

742
00:37:43,834 --> 00:37:45,795
By killing Nathan Barnes
you cheated him out of it.

743
00:37:46,712 --> 00:37:47,755
This is a live feed.

744
00:37:48,297 --> 00:37:50,007
Turn yourself in for the murder
and we'll protect you.

745
00:37:50,174 --> 00:37:54,053
Look, I don't know what this is
but this is really crazy.

746
00:37:55,346 --> 00:37:56,722
Have fun telling Holiday that.

747
00:38:09,610 --> 00:38:12,738
McInnis, come on back.

748
00:38:14,156 --> 00:38:15,199
We're waiting on you.

749
00:38:17,868 --> 00:38:18,911
Come on, son.

750
00:38:20,079 --> 00:38:21,122
It's your turn to deal.

751
00:38:23,374 --> 00:38:24,709
Come on back and play.

752
00:38:27,545 --> 00:38:28,587
Get me out of here.

753
00:38:29,630 --> 00:38:30,923
Good choice.
Let's go.

754
00:38:34,552 --> 00:38:35,594
Where you going?

755
00:38:49,900 --> 00:38:52,778
My fiancée, Heidi
started spending a lot of time

756
00:38:52,903 --> 00:38:56,115
helping Nathan
with his pro-bono legal work.

757
00:38:56,449 --> 00:38:57,992
I suspected she was cheating on me.

758
00:38:58,909 --> 00:38:59,994
I didn't have proof

759
00:39:00,119 --> 00:39:02,079
until Nathan showed up
at the game that night.

760
00:39:04,081 --> 00:39:05,875
"I was losing that night... bad."

761
00:39:06,792 --> 00:39:07,835
"Something was off."

762
00:39:08,836 --> 00:39:09,879
"Then I figured it out."

763
00:39:10,671 --> 00:39:13,382
Nathan was wearing
one of my shirts.

764
00:39:14,091 --> 00:39:15,343
How'd you know
it was your shirt?

765
00:39:16,886 --> 00:39:18,220
My monogram on the cuff.

766
00:39:18,971 --> 00:39:20,973
Nathan was sleeping with Heidi.

767
00:39:21,724 --> 00:39:24,185
Must've grabbed one of my shirts
at her apartment instead of his.

768
00:39:26,103 --> 00:39:27,605
He took a lot of money
from me that night

769
00:39:28,397 --> 00:39:30,066
and he... he smirked
when he did it.

770
00:39:30,191 --> 00:39:32,985
Ugh, that little bastard. He
was just rubbing it in my face.

771
00:39:33,319 --> 00:39:34,904
He knew I knew
and he loved it.

772
00:39:36,530 --> 00:39:37,573
"I followed him out."

773
00:39:37,948 --> 00:39:38,991
"I confronted him."

774
00:39:40,201 --> 00:39:42,661
He had the nerve to deny it...
deny all of it.

775
00:39:47,166 --> 00:39:48,501
"But he was wearing the proof."

776
00:39:51,587 --> 00:39:52,922
We spoke with your fiancée.

777
00:39:56,801 --> 00:39:59,303
Heidi had gone to coffee
with Nathan in her neighborhood that day.

778
00:39:59,762 --> 00:40:01,263
Nathan spilled coffee
on his shirt

779
00:40:01,555 --> 00:40:03,432
and she gave him one
of your clean shirts to borrow.

780
00:40:04,975 --> 00:40:08,104
The only thing he ever did
to you was beat you in cards.

781
00:40:25,246 --> 00:40:27,498
- Nice party.
- This is how we do it.

782
00:40:28,249 --> 00:40:29,291
Hey.

783
00:40:29,625 --> 00:40:30,960
- Cheers.
- Hey, where's my beer?

784
00:40:31,085 --> 00:40:33,254
Oh, Texas girls drink margaritas.

785
00:40:33,504 --> 00:40:35,047
- Give me the beer.
- Okay.

786
00:40:35,172 --> 00:40:37,925
Hey, we got, uh, burgers
brats, veggie-patty crap

787
00:40:38,050 --> 00:40:39,969
if you want veggie-patty crap.

788
00:40:40,553 --> 00:40:42,638
- Your face looks better.
- Eh, it's still a little sore.

789
00:40:44,390 --> 00:40:45,683
I know you're in trouble, Stan.

790
00:40:46,267 --> 00:40:48,352
Whatever I can do to help
let me help.

791
00:40:49,145 --> 00:40:50,187
You don't have to do that.

792
00:40:50,312 --> 00:40:51,856
I know I don't have to.
I want to.

793
00:40:52,231 --> 00:40:54,650
Just enough to keep you
from getting punched in the face again.

794
00:40:54,817 --> 00:40:57,069
I kind of thought you wouldn't mind
seeing me get punched in the face.

795
00:40:57,194 --> 00:40:58,779
I'm the only one who gets to punch you.

796
00:40:58,946 --> 00:41:00,573
- Okay. I'm good.
- You want one?

797
00:41:01,365 --> 00:41:03,742
Hey, I'm glad
you made it out.

798
00:41:04,034 --> 00:41:05,077
It means a lot.

799
00:41:05,786 --> 00:41:07,872
And Karen's family
was really impressed with you.

800
00:41:08,622 --> 00:41:09,707
I'm impressed with you.

801
00:41:10,291 --> 00:41:11,333
I'm proud of you, T.

802
00:41:11,709 --> 00:41:12,751
Thanks.

803
00:41:12,877 --> 00:41:15,045
- We should hang out more.
- Oh, like normal people?

804
00:41:15,880 --> 00:41:17,339
Yeah, like normal people.

805
00:41:17,506 --> 00:41:18,883
We should.
This has been fun.

806
00:41:19,008 --> 00:41:20,885
It's too bad Woody Squire
couldn't make it.

807
00:41:21,010 --> 00:41:22,261
- It's a real shame about that.
- Yeah.

808
00:41:22,386 --> 00:41:23,429
Shut up.

809
00:41:24,847 --> 00:41:26,098
"What's that behind your ear?"

810
00:41:26,807 --> 00:41:28,017
We talked about Patrick.

811
00:41:28,225 --> 00:41:29,894
- You did, did you?
- Yeah.

812
00:41:30,102 --> 00:41:31,145
We like him.

813
00:41:32,146 --> 00:41:33,189
He's a good guy.

814
00:41:33,772 --> 00:41:34,982
Don't mess this one up, okay?

815
00:41:39,028 --> 00:41:40,070
I'll try not to.

816
00:41:47,411 --> 00:41:48,787
I'm glad we came back home.

817
00:41:49,788 --> 00:41:51,415
Me too.
It was nice.

818
00:41:54,418 --> 00:41:56,795
I don't think I've said this.

819
00:41:57,087 --> 00:41:59,965
I mean, I know I haven't said this

820
00:42:00,132 --> 00:42:01,926
but I don't really know
if I need to

821
00:42:02,051 --> 00:42:03,969
because you always know
what I'm thinking.

822
00:42:04,428 --> 00:42:05,554
Well, not everything.

823
00:42:08,557 --> 00:42:11,477
Would you be surprised
if I said I love you?

824
00:42:13,020 --> 00:42:14,063
I'd be...

825
00:42:15,648 --> 00:42:18,901
I'd be lying if I didn't say
I would be moved by that.

826
00:42:21,820 --> 00:42:22,863
I love you.

827
00:42:27,701 --> 00:42:28,744
I said it.

828
00:42:34,291 --> 00:42:35,334
I'm surprised.

